FUNCTION NullLog(LogNumber : INTEGER) : BOOLEAN;
Checks if specified log entry has no data in any of five pointer fields. Works with internal log data structure, returns TRUE if all pointers are zero.

FUNCTION NullLog(LogNumber : INTEGER) : BOOLEAN;

  BEGIN
    WITH Log[LogNumber] DO
      NullLog:=
        (Pointer[TRt]<=0) AND
        (Pointer[Deliveryt]<=0) AND
        (Pointer[DLMFIt]<=0) AND
        (Pointer[MMPt]<=0) AND
        (Pointer[Pricet]<=0);
  END;

